% Scenario: the array, packed-array, and string operators; forall runs as
% a loop frame so exit leaves it; setpacking governs scanned procedures
% only; a store into a global array of a local value is rejected.
2 array ==
[ 1 2 3 ] ==
[ 4 5 6 ] aload pop add add =
1 2 3 3 array astore length =
(abcdef) 2 2 getinterval ==
(abcdef) dup 1 (XY) putinterval ==
[ 1 2 ] { = } forall
<< /b 1 >> { = == } forall
(ab) { = } forall
[ 1 2 3 4 ] { dup 3 eq { exit } if pop } forall =
(hello) (l) search dup = { == == == } { == } ifelse
(hello) (x) search dup = { == == == } { == } ifelse
(hello) (hel) anchorsearch dup = { == == } { == } ifelse
1 2 2 packedarray type ==
true setpacking { 1 } type == false setpacking [ 1 ] type == { 1 } type ==
true setglobal 1 array false setglobal
{ 0 (local) put } stopped pop $error /errorname get ==
